  "assumptions": [
    "Every machine, speed, resolution, limit and network parameter below is an illustrative engineering input, not a confirmed user requirement or a measured device capability.",
    "One commanded step pulse advances the drive by one configured input increment; drive electronic gearing is already included in drive_input_pulses_per_motor_rev.",
    "motor_revs_per_output_rev is motor revolutions divided by output revolutions. Linear output_mm_per_rev describes screw lead or belt travel per output revolution.",
    "All joints are assumed to reach their configured maxima simultaneously for the aggregate upper-demand example. Direction-change timing, pulse quantization, reversals and acceleration scheduling are excluded.",
    "Quadrature lines are decoded at four counts per line; decoded counts and single-channel rising pulses receive no extra factor of four.",
    "The modeled wired packet slot uses explicitly configured byte counts, including padding and interpacket gap. It assumes no VLAN, encryption, tunneling, fragmentation, retransmission or additional traffic.",
    "Stopping examples assume constant speed during the stated reaction interval and immediate constant deceleration afterward; they are not measured stops, worst-case bounds, safety distances or an emergency-stop design."
  ],
